# Testing Standards

## BDDMockito Style Requirements

### Import Statements
- **Use**: `import static org.mockito.BDDMockito.given;`
- **Use**: `import static org.mockito.BDDMockito.verify;`
- **Use**: `import static org.mockito.BDDMockito.willDoNothing;`
- **Avoid**: `import static org.mockito.BDDMockito.willReturn;` (use `given().willReturn()` instead)

### Mock Setup Pattern
```java
// Correct BDDMockito style
given(this.service.methodCall()).willReturn(expectedResult);
given(this.repository.findById(any())).willReturn(Optional.of(entity));

// For void methods
willDoNothing().given(this.service).voidMethod();

// For exceptions
given(this.service.methodCall()).willThrow(new RuntimeException("Error"));
```

### Verification Pattern
```java
// Correct BDDMockito style
verify(this.service).methodCall();
verify(this.repository).save(any(Entity.class));
verify(this.apiResponder).respond(any(), eq("Success message"));
```

## Test Structure

### Class Annotations
```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
@DisplayName("ServiceName Tests")
class ServiceNameTests {
    // Test implementation
}
```

### Mock Declarations
```java
@Mock
private ServiceInterface service;

@Mock
private RepositoryInterface repository;

@InjectMocks
private ServiceImplementation serviceImpl;
```

### Test Method Naming
- **Format**: `test[MethodName]_[Scenario]_[ExpectedResult]`
- **Example**: `testCreateTimesheet_validInput_createsTimesheet()`
- **Example**: `testGetTimesheetById_invalidId_throwsResourceNotFoundException()`

### Test Method Structure
```java
@Test
@DisplayName("Method description - Success")
void testMethodNameSuccess() {
    // Arrange
    given(this.dependency.method()).willReturn(result);
    
    // Act
    ResultType result = this.service.methodCall();
    
    // Assert
    assertThat(result).isEqualTo(expectedResult);
    verify(this.dependency).method();
}
```

## Assertion Patterns

### Using AssertJ
```java
// Basic assertions
assertThat(result).isNotNull();
assertThat(result).isEqualTo(expectedValue);
assertThat(result).hasSize(2);

// Exception assertions
assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.methodCall())
    .isInstanceOf(ValidationErrorException.class)
    .hasMessage("Expected error message");
```

### Collection Assertions
```java
assertThat(list).hasSize(2);
assertThat(list).contains(expectedItem);
assertThat(list).extracting("fieldName").containsOnly(expectedValues);
```

## Test Data Management

### Mock Data Creation
```java
// Use Mockito.mock() for complex objects
SearchRequestBodyDto searchRequest = mock(SearchRequestBodyDto.class);
Pageable pageable = mock(Pageable.class);

// Use builders for simple objects
TimesheetRequestDto request = TimesheetRequestDto.builder()
    .name("Test Timesheet")
    .candidateId(123)
    .build();
```

### Test Data Builders
```java
public class TestDataBuilder {
    public static TimesheetRequestDto createTimesheetRequest() {
        return new TimesheetRequestDto(
            "Test Timesheet",
            123,
            456,
            LocalDate.now(),
            List.of()
        );
    }
}
```

## Integration Test Patterns

### Controller Integration Tests
```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = AutoConfigureTestDatabase.Replace.NONE)
class ControllerIntegrationTests {
    
    @Autowired
    private TestRestTemplate restTemplate;
    
    @Test
    void testEndpoint_integration() {
        // Test implementation
    }
}
```

